  "step_3": "The decision reason requires the individual to: (1) identify probable outcomes using a threshold of 1/n (n = 2 here, so >0.5), and (2) compute the average of those probable outcomes and prefer the lottery with the higher average. The individual does not mention the threshold, does not identify probable outcomes based on probability >0.5, and does not calculate or compare the average of probable outcomes. Instead, the justification is based on a subjective hope of winning (i.e., getting 0 Euros), which is not aligned with the formal rule of the decision reason. Therefore, the individual did not apply the decision reason. The reasoning is qualitatively different and lacks the structural elements of the reason. There is no evidence of using the rule for evaluating probable outcomes or their average. Hence, the decision reason was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
}

