  "step_3": "The decision reason requires: (1) identifying probable outcomes (probabilities > 1/n), and (2) computing the average of those probable outcomes and comparing them. The individual did not identify or categorize outcomes as probable according to the defined threshold (1/n). The individual’s justification is based on a subjective feeling of needing 'double the luck' in A, which is not equivalent to evaluating probable outcomes or their average. There is no mention of probabilities above 1/3 or 1/2, nor of comparing averages of probable outcomes. Therefore, the individual did not apply the decision reason. The reasoning is qualitatively different and does not match the structure or content of the decision reason. Hence, the decision reason was not used.",
